{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cfb9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06fb9-e0fc-7072-adfc-69f8598926a4"},"sequence":1591,"recorded_at":1780531400003177,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"694249df-ed90-4909-b924-7901358b9328","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"694249df-ed90-4909-b924-7901358b9328","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"694249df-ed90-4909-b924-7901358b9328"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"6270eb6e-2ab5-4843-a976-b98d2a2f3c8d"},"task_id":"6270eb6e-2ab5-4843-a976-b98d2a2f3c8d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"6270eb6e-2ab5-4843-a976-b98d2a2f3c8d","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-44-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '585,613p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read latest LOGBOOK entry style\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"- STATUS: BUG-260902-beqfwr on `task-board/story/STORY-260902-2230n7`, one commit past checkpoint `6f77719`; `internal/config` coverage 93.7% (measured at the checkpoint) -> 93.9%; `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l .`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `go test ./... -cover`, tracecheck, and the catalog `-check` gate all exit 0; ten single-clause mutants each redden their own cases; handed off to review.\\n\\n### 0900 — BUG-260902-lyhvkw rev-2 reapplied onto advanced trunk a351afd\\n- FINDING: the accepted revision-2 patch reapplied cleanly except `internal/traceability/traceability.go`, where trunk had independently repinned `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256`; resolved to the trunk value, then repinned to the recomputed projection digest `9f7737cb07f853012fcc9e2359981e20e9b65df622f9da7fa4935a2180cd04b0` reported by tracecheck.\\n- STATUS: canonicaljson coverage 87.1% (trunk a351afd) -> 87.2%; widen-512, narrow-128, and delete-gate mutants all redden the suite; the delete-gate mutant still reproduces `fatal error: stack overflow`.\\n\\n### 0500 — A vocabulary gate that refuses one outside value proves nothing about the admitted set\\n\\n- FINDING: a derived mutation sweep that admitted **one extra member** at each of the 47 closed-vocabulary call sites in `internal/canonicaljson` survived **47 out of 47 times**. `go test ./...`, all four seeded fuzz corpora, `tracecheck`, the derived declared-bounds inventory and the derived refusal-guard coverage gate were all green while, for example, `validateLeaseRecord` admitted a fifth lease reason and `validateObservationEvent` admitted a sixth result.\\n- ROOT CAUSE: every vocabulary had a \\\"refuses a value outside the vocabulary\\\" negative, which proves the gate is REACHABLE, not that the admitted set is the DECLARED set. Coverage cannot separate the two: a widened gate still executes its refusal for whichever outside value the test picked. This is the same shape as the bounds finding one round earlier — an obligation that does not carry the literal cannot fail when the literal moves.\\n- FIX: `internal/canonicaljson/closed_vocabularies_test.go` derives the vocabulary-admitting helpers from the sources (a function that yields the value it admitted and decides admission from its own variadic set, plus any wrapper forwarding that set to one), derives every call site with its member and admitted values in declaration order, and pins the result against a reviewed `testdata/closed-vocabularies.md` that cites the SPEC line declaring each vocabulary. Widening, narrowing, reordering, an unpinned call site and a deleted row all fail — at derivation, before any case runs. 47/47 mutants now killed.\\n- NOTE: the helper set is asserted complete, so a second copy of `requireEnum` reddens rather than quietly carrying unpinned vocabularies. Proven, not asserted: a duplicate helper in a new production file was added and the gate named it.\\n- FINDING, same sweep: three refusal guards in `core_records.go` were proven by one witness each where the guard has several disjuncts — the `opaque_identity` and logical-identity absolute-path guards were proven only by a POSIX `/` prefix, so dropping the UNC and drive-letter disjuncts stayed green, and the `session.stopped` **checkpointed** arm was proven only by a null checkpoint, so dropping `!resumable` stayed green. Each now has one isolated negative per disjunct at both identity entries.\\n- SCOPE, measured and disclosed rather than fixed: the same two derived sweeps were pointed at `canonical.go` and `closed_shapes.go`, the preceding leaves, because \\\"we did not look\\\" and \\\"there is nothing there\\\" are different facts. 262 mutants, 200 killed, 12 not compilable, **50 survivors**. All 18 guard-deletion survivors are equivalent mutants already declared in `unreachableRefusalSites` with a subsuming refusal and a named proving test, matched return-by-return. The other **32 are real one-directional proofs** in the preceding leaves — an equality coupling with a counterpart on one lexical side only, and a strictly-sorted list proven by reversal but never by a duplicate. Both shapes were claimed closed for `core_records.go` in that revision. The full per-survivor list, with what each mutant silently admits, ships as `TASK-260830-1tax26_rev4-preceding-leaf-survivors.md`; the natural owner is the sibling `TASK-260830-uqnwmi`, whose deliverable is exactly this conformance-test class.\\n- CORRECTION (2026-09-02, revision 6): \\\"Both shapes are closed for `core_records.go` in this revision\\\" does not reproduce and is corrected above. The revision-4 grammar rewrote comparison OPERATORS, which cannot express either of the two shapes review then found in `core_records.go`: a boolean-valued `!=` has no operator to rewrite, only a boolean identity to split into `a && !b` / `!a && b`; and `epoch != 1` narrowed to `epoch > 1` is an equivalent mutant, so the operator sweep provably could not reach the `epoch >= 3` narrowing that admitted an epoch-2 lease with a null predecessor. The honest revision-4 claim is: the one-directional EQUALITY-COUPLING shape the operator grammar could express was closed for `core_records.go`; the boolean-identity and literal-boundary shapes were never swept there. Both are closed in revision 6 by standing derived gates, not by a sweep.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/canonicaljson/`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md`\\n- STATUS: Resolved in revision 4.\\n\\n\\n### 0420 — Canonical decode nesting depth capped at 256\\n- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/canonicaljson/canonical.go` `decodeValue` recursed once per nesting level with no bound; a 2,000,000-byte document of one million nested arrays exhausted the goroutine stack and killed the process with uncatchable `fatal error: stack overflow` at `Canonicalize`, `CalculateObjectIdentity`, and `VerifyObjectIdentity`, well under the 5,242,880-byte identity size cap.\\n- FIX: `maxNestingDepth = 256` (`internal/canonicaljson/canonical.go:37`) enforced inside `decodeValue` before it opens a container (`canonical.go:362`), typed `ErrInvalidJSON`; every public entry inherits it through the shared `decodeStrict`.\\n- DECISION: 256 chosen because the deepest pinned closed shape (16-level submodule tree) decodes at roughly depth 40 and open extensions stop at depth 4, giving more than sixfold headroom; the bound stays far below encoding/json's 10,000-level cap and jcs's unbounded re-parse, so the typed refusal is always the first gate a deep document meets.\\n- FINDING: the delete-gate mutant reproduces the exact crash (`runtime: goroutine stack exceeds 1000000000-byte limit`, exit 1 with fatal error) through the new regression test; widen-512 and narrow-128 mutants both redden the suite because tests pin the literal 256/257 rather than reading the constant.\\n- FINDING: registering new evidence tests in `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` requires repinning `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in `internal/traceability/traceability.go:42`; tracecheck fails closed on the projection digest until the repin is reviewed.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/canonicaljson/canonical.go`, `internal/canonicaljson/nesting_depth_test.go`, `internal/canonicaljson/testdata/constraint-enumeration.md`, `internal/canonicaljson/testdata/fuzz/FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip/nesting-depth-over-limit`, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json`, `internal/traceability/traceability.go`, `README.md`.\\n- STATUS: fixed in STORY-260902-3os1kh workspace (trunk 48db30b descendant); canonicaljson coverage 87.1% -> 87.2%; handed off to review.\\n\\n### 0130 — Coverage is the only honest proof that a gate was reached\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7564,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1891,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
