{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cfe1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06fb9-e0fc-7072-adfc-69f8598926a4"},"sequence":1611,"recorded_at":1780531400003217,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"694249df-ed90-4909-b924-7901358b9328","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"694249df-ed90-4909-b924-7901358b9328","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"694249df-ed90-4909-b924-7901358b9328"},"call_id":"call_01a06fc71bcb775098e73d695b7b489a","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-45-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '1,40p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK head format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-05\\n\\n### 0510 — Provider conformance-harness leaf: operation decoders, derived complements, inventory census 60 → 162\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti (final leaf of STORY-260830-3jqsx1). New `internal/provhost` operation layer: manifest (7.3), probe + capability gate (7.4/8.3), profile mapping (7.7), quiescence proof (7.6), SpawnPlan for launch/resume, Provider Identity Record + identify result (5.5), and the single `(operation, operation_id)` key (7.5), with Host.Call conformance sequences (manifest/probe/resume/identify/quiesce end to end, 21 fail-closed capability-by-status tuples with zero processes started, byte-identical lost-prepare retry, changed-body `idempotency_mismatch` passthrough, child-code passthrough table). Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- MECHANISM (leaf-2 item closed here): the derived refusal-arm inventory parses production AST — every `&frameFault` literal, every literal `integrity(...)` argument (with the `decodeStrictObject`-fault wrapper expanded over the derived frame detail set), every `parseMajor` rejection branch keyed by enclosing condition, and every literal first argument to the six refusal constructors — and checks both directions (every derived arm witnessed, every witness derived) plus a census floor. This leaf raised the floor 60 → 162 and added 102 witnesses, one per new arm.\\n- BLIND SHAPES (stated, not fixed): a one-line wrapper fronting a constructor and an aliased constructor at an unexercised site are both invisible to the arm walk and the site audit; both measured empty in this tree and neither shape was introduced. The file header's \\\"non-literal shapes never silent\\\" line was corrected: constructor non-literals are fault conduits by design, not obligations.\\n- CENSUS-FLOOR REASONING: the floor catches a silently truncated scan (empty, single-file, or short derivation fails even when every surviving arm is witnessed); the reverse witness check catches a deleted or narrowed production branch by orphaning its witness. Raising is routine with new refusals; lowering requires saying why.\\n- DEFECT (caught by the new tests, fixed before review): the first `DecodeQuiesceProof` draft omitted both open counts from the safe-rule disjunction — `safe:true` with `open_child_count:1` validated. The per-conjunct safe-lie fixtures (one violated fact each) caught it; counts now return through `checkQuiesceCounts` into the rule.\\n- COMPLEMENTS, NOT SAMPLES: 6 providers × 2 profiles swept; 4 statuses × 2 enabled swept for the probe rule, the pure gate, and one capability key, plus a per-key sweep over all 7 registry keys; keyed operations derived per-row from the Section 7.5 table (capture, materialize, commit, rollback, fork) with the 10 unkeyed operations refused in the same test; registries (operations, capabilities, platforms) re-derived from the Section 7.3 example.\\n- EVIDENCE: 26 narrowing mutants (order-skip-first, bound+1, grammar weakening, gate `&&`→`||`, disjunct drops, key widening, registry deletion), each presence-asserted, full-package run, cp-aside restore byte-verified, tree hash equal before/after: 24 killed on first run, 2 survived (order checks skipping index 0 — no fixture distinguished the first element), both killed after adding first-element-substitution fixtures. Final: 26/26, 0 survivors. `go test ./...` exit 0, `-race` on provhost exit 0, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 unchanged (17/403, 74 cases — no ownership bindings added or claimed). provhost cover 86.4% (was 88.1%: the new decoders add the same constructor-error propagation branches the audit already records as the uncovered remainder).\\n- BOUNDS (unchanged and restated): `provhost` still has no importers and imports no new package; no top-level `cmd/`; the ten leaf-2 survivors stay as stated (S11/S12/S13/U2 included — no test implies detached-descendant knowledge); S1's one-off ExecRunner fork/exec red stands recorded. New bounds: mutation receipts live in the transaction document/plugin (host holds no cache — cross-crash durability is the document's property); Section 8 cell values are evidence labels (host pins the fail-closed direction per tuple, not per cell); Section 8.2 store exclusions, commit/rollback result vocabularies, and remaining Section 7.5 request bodies are still opaque; literal secrecy and shell-string argv rules are structural, not content-admitted; record_id is shape-checked, not recomputed.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0435 — Provider JSONL host leaf round-2 rework: arm identity, exact bounds, production-site pins\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-qcosxq round-1 verdict (changes requested, 44/66 killed, 18 real survivors). Test-only rework in `internal/provhost` plus README/LOGBOOK honesty items; production untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F25, structural, first): every refusal row now names its arm — `requireFrameRefusal` (code + `member` detail + rule detail + non-retryable) for frame refusals, `requireLocalRefusal` (code + rule detail + non-retryable) for invalid_config/integrity/timeout/process arms, plus `observed`-version assertions on both mismatch paths and `status_state` on unknown. Zero code-only refusal rows remain outside the two helpers, the bound-child surfacing check, and mismatch checks paired with identity assertions. Matches the sibling leaf's 0/29 → all-asserted shape.\\n- FIX (F21): five foreign-major malformed versions (`3.0`, `3.0.0.0`, `.0.0`, `3..0`, `3.b.c`) asserting `provider_protocol_error`; each of the four deleted `parseMajor` arms now promotes its shape to `incompatible_protocol` and reddens.\\n- FIX (F22): token floor pinned two-sided — 31 decoded bytes refused, 32 accepted. Floors `< 8`, `< 16` killed by the 31-byte row; `< 48` killed by the 32-byte row and the 38-byte valid fixture.\\n- FIX (F23): `readCapped` cap path tested both halves — over-cap cut to exactly cap bytes with prefix content (kills truncation removal), error-past-the-cap never reached (kills limiter removal), under/exact-cap passthrough.\\n- FIX (F24): request side gains the exact-boundary test the response side had — limit+1 refused with arm identity, limit accepted. Halving the request bound reddens.\\n- FIX (F26): `exit 3` / `exit 0` silent plugins driven through production `ExecRunner` + `Host.Call`; the both-sites-cleared exit-code mutant reproduces the reviewer's exact `process_failed` → `protocol_error` flip and is killed.\\n- FIX (F27): stdin capture through production `ExecRunner` asserts frame + one `\\\\n`; the omitted-terminator mutant reddens.\\n- FIX (F28/F29): orphaned discovery paragraph moved back above the JSONL section; the \\\"proven by narrowing mutants\\\" sentence restated to what the tests pin (arm identities, 31/32 token bytes, both exact frame bounds).\\n- FINDING: the crash-exit test as first written was flaky — a plugin that exits without draining stdin races stdin writes into EPIPE, surfacing `runner reported no result` instead of the exit-code path. Fixed by draining stdin in the fixture scripts; the flake is in the fixture, not production.\\n- EQUIVALENT (declared, not chased): M09b — narrowing the `checkResponseMembers` required list to drop `\\\"ok\\\"` changes nothing observable, because the missing-`ok` pre-check in `DecodeResponse` fires first on every input missing `ok`. The list entry is unreachable defense in depth. Single-site R17 (clearing only the `ExitError`-branch reassignment) is likewise a no-op because the `Result` literal already carries `ProcessState.ExitCode()`; the behavior-bearing mutant clears both sites and is killed.\\n- EVIDENCE: 19-mutant verify sweep (`/tmp/rev2-verify.sh`, cp-aside/cp-back per mutant, presence asserted, restore byte-verified): 18 killed, 1 declared equivalent (M09b). True two-site R17 verified killed separately with the reviewer's exact flip. `go test ./...` exit 0 (15/15), `-race` on provhost exit 0, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt gate clean, `go build` on linux/windows exit 0, `tracecheck` exit 0 unchanged (17/403, 74 cases). provhost cover 86.1% → 88.1%.\\n- BOUND (stated plainly, widened the wrong way): `provhost` does not import `internal/provider` (only a comment at `runner.go:44`), so this leaf is not the first production caller; `provhost` itself has no production caller and there is no `cmd/ax`. Two orphaned packages, every `Host.Call` assertion made from a test. The non-retryability sentence in `doc.go` is now asserted on every refusal row rather than standing on prose.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0429 — Provider JSONL host leaf: protocol transport, three inherited findings, one repeated harness failure\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-qcosxq (story leaf 2). New `internal/provhost` (§7.2 framing/lifecycle, §7.5 dispatch names, status recovery; bodies opaque except status rules), plus F18/F19/F20 closures in `internal/provider` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FINDING: F18 closed with the verdict's four-line pin (`ownerAttester` pointer-equals `fileOwnerUID`); SEAM1 verified red before restore. F19 closed by planting a distinct-ID candidate in each absolute dir of `TestDiscoverRefusesRelativePluginDir`; the `return out` mutant returns 1 candidate and reddens. F20 closed with a `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` CI step; a planted type error in `os_windows_test.go` verified the step sees the file.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9590,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2398,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
